    "updated_at": "2025-08-20T14:07:10Z",
    "body": "> You mean something like this? Not sure. Does this work for implicit label or submit refs?\n\n```html\n<dialog>\n  <custom-foo>\n<template shadowrootmode=open>\n     <button command=close>Close</button>\n  </template>\n</custom-foo>\n</dialog>\n```\n\nYeah, I just checked and it seems like label implicit for, and form element implicit form owner both don't cross shadow boundaries, https://codepen.io/lukewarlow/pen/EaVERPq\n\nI suspect changing those might be compat risky at this point, but doesn't mean that this new idea should definitely have the same limitation.\n\nI guess for implicit for, you can do the below with reference target to half get there, but there's no proposal to solve escaping upwards yet via HTML so can't do the form relationship nor this implicit commandfor close stuff.\n\n```html\n<label> Label\n  <custom-element>\n    <template shadowrootmode=\"open\" shadowrootreferencetarget=\"input\">\n      <input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"input\">\n    </template>\n  </custom-element>\n</label>\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
