    "updated_at": "2025-08-20T14:11:06Z",
    "body": "At first glance seems reasonable to automatically map the given command to an implicit flat tree ancestor, such that `command=close` would walk the flat tree for a `<dialog>` and `command=show-popover` would walk the flat tree for a `popover` element.\n\nThere are some difficulties it introduces, however. The [\"Invoker Commands Future\"](https://open-ui.org/components/future-invokers.explainer/) explainer proposes that `'close'` could be a command for `<details>` elements. Re-using command names makes sense in the context of the current proposal introduces complexities in combination with this proposal: does `'close'` find the nearest `<details>` _or_ `<dialog>`? Does this become confusing for developers?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/3206589757/reactions",
