    "body": "> At first glance seems reasonable to automatically map the given command to an implicit flat tree ancestor, such that `command=close` would walk the flat tree for a `<dialog>` and `command=show-popover` would walk the flat tree for a `popover` element.\n> \n> There are some difficulties it introduces, however. The [\"Invoker Commands Future\"](https://open-ui.org/components/future-invokers.explainer/) explainer proposes that `'close'` could be a command for `<details>` elements. Re-using command names makes sense in the context of the current proposal introduces complexities in combination with this proposal: does `'close'` find the nearest `<details>` _or_ `<dialog>`? Does this become confusing for developers?\n\nProbably the nearest closable? There is always an option to use IDs but at least some of the simple cases don't require them.",
